sd: a click on a script URL keeps room for its target

SdUnoEventsAccess::getByName sizes its property sequence before it
fills it. For a PROGRAM, VERB, BOOKMARK or DOCUMENT click it made
room for the target only when the target was not a script URL, a
test that belongs to MACRO alone, but it then wrote the target
anyway, past the end of the sequence. A PPTX hlinkClick to
vnd.sun.star.script:… imports as a DOCUMENT click, so exporting the
deck's events (ODF save, XMLShapeExport::ImpExportEvents) overran
the heap and the process died in rtl_uString_assign (Ely R20.50).

Those four clicks now always make room for their target.

diff --git a/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unoobj.cxx b/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unoobj.cxx
--- a/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unoobj.cxx
+++ b/sd/source/ui/unoidl/unoobj.cxx
@@ -1439,6 +1439,9 @@
     case presentation::ClickAction_VERB:
     case presentation::ClickAction_BOOKMARK:
     case presentation::ClickAction_DOCUMENT:
+        // Ely: these write one more property, script URL or not.
+        nPropertyCount += 1;
+        break;
     case presentation::ClickAction_MACRO:
         if ( !SfxApplication::IsXScriptURL( pInfo->GetBookmark() ) )
             nPropertyCount += 1;
